Date: Wed, 26 Aug 2026 17:48:17 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] dos: rename 8.3-unsafe filenames + sync
 g_dos_sfx_synth_active_count

Several of Passage's own filenames exceed the DOS 8.3 (8-char name +
3-char extension) limit and would truncate or fail to open on real
MS-DOS (no LFN driver) -- same issue class as doskutsu's own
patches/nxengine-evo/0033-0035 8.3-rename precedent. Renamed both the
files and every string-literal reference to them:

graphics/:
  characterSprite.tga    -> charspr.tga
  characterSpriteSad.tga -> charsad.tga
  spouseSprite.tga       -> spouse.tga
  chestPrize.tga         -> cprize.tga
  chestDust.tga          -> cdust.tga
(tileSet.tga, chest.tga, heart.tga, numerals.tga, title.tga, and
music/music.tga were already 8.3-compliant -- left unchanged.)

settings/ (setting names double as the .ini basename, per minorGems'
SettingsManager::getSettingsFileName -- renaming the file alone isn't
enough, the string passed to getIntSetting() must match):
  screenWidth  -> width   (settings/width.ini)
  screenHeight -> height  (settings/height.ini)
  fullscreen   -> fullscrn (settings/fullscrn.ini)

The C++ variable names screenWidth/screenHeight in game.cpp are
unrelated identifiers, not filenames -- left unchanged.

Also (unrelated concern, bundled here rather than as a third patch
since it's a one-line rename): renamed g_pixtone_active_count ->
g_dos_sfx_synth_active_count in game.cpp, following the shared
SDL3-DOS backend's own generic-ification of that extern
(sdl-dos-ports commit 9e9c5a8, fixed for real in 6647fc8 after a
regression -- this port's .sdl-dos-ports submodule pin bumped to
6647fc8 to match). See patch 0001's commit message for why this
symbol needs to exist here at all.

Verified: builds clean, boots to title screen and gameplay under
DOSBox-X with lfn=false (real-MS-DOS-representative).

